  "outcome": {
    "ok": true,
    "turn_id": "d09_final_matched:r8:t6",
    "narration": "Iris sits on one of the simple stools near the nearest bed, her posture unhurried. The floor is quiet — just the two of them and the sparse furnishing of the observation floor, beds with their bare nightstands and empty wardrobes along one side, the closed wooden cabinets opposite. Light from the perimeter windows falls across the open central space.\n\nShe waits a beat after the question, looking toward the stair access as though checking that the quiet still holds. \"You've been doing most of the talking,\" she says. Her tone carries no reproach — just observation. \"I don't mind listening. But if you're asking what I'd like…\" She pauses again. \"I don't have much to add yet. I'm still figuring out what this place is, what you want from it.\"\n\nShe looks back toward him. \"So maybe that's my answer. Tell me what you're planning. Then I'll know whether I have something to say about it.\"",
